From f26c48d3f2e32a0db28e55a4aaa00edbb704e588 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Buckley <10402042+ryancbuckley@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 15:59:11 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Clippy built into rustc for WASI hosts (RUSTC_CLIPPY=1)

Without dylibs, a separate clippy-driver would be a second copy of the whole
compiler. On WASI, rustc links Clippy's lints instead, and registers them
the way clippy-driver does when RUSTC_CLIPPY is set (compiler/rustc/src/
clippy.rs). Clippy's crates get Cargo dependencies on the compiler crates
they use through extern crate, so that they build with the compiler.
